       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Single doses are generally 1,000 mg or less.\n- **Risk:** The ordered total is about twice the maximum. That raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- Another dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll reconsider. I'd also suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
