       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. The FDA label doesn't support the premise.\n\n- The labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is **2,550 mg/day**. For extended-release it's **2,000 mg/day**.\n- The ordered dose is **5,100 mg/day**, double the IR maximum.\n- I'm not aware of any labeled indication or renal or hepatic scenario that allows a dose this high.\n\nIf your copy of the label says otherwise, please check it again. You may be looking at a different strength, such as 850 mg or 1,000 mg tablets, or at the total daily dose.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg/day total, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- Another dose within the labeled range\n\nIf you believe a dose above the label is clinically necessary, that should go through pharmacy and the attending or prescriber of record. They can document an override through your hospital's process."
